WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.440
Schizophrenic mutant David Haller from FX's
Legion — based on the X-Men character of

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.270
the same name — is played by an English
actor you swear you've seen before.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:12.510
Dan Stevens has popped up to steal scenes
in a wide variety of well-received, unusual

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.020
and offbeat projects in the last decade or
so, making him one of those actors that's

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.150
hard to place.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.940
Why is he so familiar?

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.640
Stevens got his very first onscreen credit
in the miniseries Frankenstein in 2004, and

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.870
continued popping up in TV adaptations of
classic works over the next few years, such

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:34.839
as Dracula in 2006, Sense and Sensibility
in 2008, and The Turn of the Screw in 2009.

00:00:34.839 --> 00:00:38.019
Stevens says he had done quite a few period
dramas at this point and was ready not to

00:00:38.019 --> 00:00:41.350
do another one, which brings us to ... another
one.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:46.309
Stevens' big breakthrough came in 2010 when
he landed his as the lovable cousin Matthew

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:50.329
Crawley in the beloved BBC costume drama Downton
Abbey.

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:55.000
Yep: Stevens almost didn't take the gig that
shot him up to stardom, but he says the well-crafted

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.079
relationship between Matthew and Lady Mary
compelled him to get on board.

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:01.499
"You've shown me I've been living in a dream.

00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:06.070
And it's time to return to real life.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:07.899
Wish me luck with it, Mary."

00:01:07.899 --> 00:01:11.380
Stevens played Matthew to much acclaim for
three seasons before departing the show in

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.770
an unexpected fashion that disappointed many
Downton fans.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:19.400
Shortly after his exit from the Abbey, Stevens
appeared on the big screen in 2013's The Fifth

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:24.930
Estate, a fictionalized account of the founding
of the ever-controversial online outfit Wikileaks.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:29.479
Playing a small but important role opposite
fellow English heartthrob Benedict Cumberbatch,

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:32.130
Stevens played Ian Katz, a real-life editor
from the Guardian.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:36.280
"Anyone can take a bundle of information and
toss it up on a website and call it news.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.929
People buy our papers for something a little
more discerning."

00:01:38.929 --> 00:01:42.100
"People still buying your paper?"

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:47.289
Next, Stevens appeared in two standout installments
of the character-driven series High Maintenance,

00:01:47.289 --> 00:01:51.649
playing a cross-dressing stay-at-home dad,
stoner, and struggling writer named Colin.

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:54.000
"Can I top anyone off?"

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.000
“I’m good.”

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.350
"I love this."

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.350
"Oh this?

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.350
Thank you."

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:02.479
Stevens appeared both in an episode in the
original web-based run in 2014 and the second

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:07.109
episode of the HBO incarnation, landing the
gig after publicly praising the series as

00:02:07.109 --> 00:02:10.750
"brilliant" in his monthly column for the
Telegraph in 2013.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.720
Stevens had a busy year in 2014.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.830
One of his most memorable film roles came
in Adam Wingard's fantastic thriller The Guest,

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.170
where he plays an intensely charming but very
bad man.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.980
Employing deadly fighting skills and a flawless
American accent …

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.940
"Get him out of here."

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.740
… Stevens plays an ex-military houseguest
with an unknown past who charms his way into

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.210
a family's good graces, looking like the best
thing to ever happen to them … before the

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.080
dark, disturbing truth comes out.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.770
Stevens also has a role in one of Adam Sandler's
weirdest movies, The Cobbler.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:47.530
It's about a shoe repairman with an inexplicably
magical stitching machine who can literally

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:49.950
become another person if he wears their shoes.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.040
The poorly -received 2014 film does provide
viewers with the distinct pleasure of watching

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.470
Stevens play Adam-Sandler-in-another-body,
an unusually layered acting challenge ...

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.610
"Get in here, cute boy."

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:01.610
"Me?

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.610
Really?

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.610
In there?"

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.610
"Yeah."

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:05.610
"With you?"

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.220
"Really.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:07.220
Your friends can wait."

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:08.600
"Oh yeah."

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.710
But when he wasn't hanging out with Adam Sandler,
Stevens found himself acting opposite Liam

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:16.510
Neeson in the meditative 2014 crime drama
A Walk Among the Tombstones.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:20.450
Stevens plays a man named Kenny Kristo who
enlists Neeson's ex-cop character to help

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.450
him solve a mystery ...

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:22.770
"Someone kidnapped my wife."

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.680
"When did this happen?"

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.680
"Yesterday."

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.480
"You should be talking to the F.B.I."

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.930
"I'm talking to you."

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:34.420
It's another change in look and accent for
Stevens — a big departure from his dressed-up

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.550
Downton days.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:40.330
But that was nothing compared to his final
big role in 2014: Night at the Museum: Secret

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.330
of the Tomb.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:45.210
For the second Night at the Museum sequel
Stevens joined an eclectic cast of historical

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:48.810
figures come to life as Sir Lancelot, and
his performance steals the show ...

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.940
"Theodore Roosevelt, President of the United
States of America."

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:55.090
"I have no idea what that means!"

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:59.050
Stevens plays the Arthurian legend as an affable
dimwit in search of the Holy Grail, with stops

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:02.900
along the way to battle and tame re-animated
dinosaur skeletons.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.790
Most recently, Stevens was instrumental in
bringing Disney's animated classic Beauty

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.530
and the Beast to live-action, playing the
Beast to Emma Watson's Belle in this 2017

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:12.530
adaptation.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.950
Aside from the opening scenes prior to his
transformation, Stevens spends most of the

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:20.310
movie as a computer-generated creation — but
the animators didn't do all the work.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:24.320
Stevens had to essentially perform the role
twice, once on the physical set, doing body

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.880
work while wearing stilts, and once alone,
surrounded by cameras capturing every nuance

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:29.880
of his face.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.260
"Have you really read every one of these books?"

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.419
"Some of them are in Greek."

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:38.980
The result was a performance hailed by Variety
as "alive with forlorn longing," with Stevens

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.260
playing the Beast as "a kind of royal version
of the Elephant Man" … proving yet again

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.910
that his talents ... are legion.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:46.960
Thanks for watching!

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.280
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.720
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

